// The city epidemic model (examples/epidemic) with the illness passed
// on: 5,000 people in households taken from a panel (city.ent: a file
// read and parsed, households kept where they fit the country's ages and
// sizes), five networks of work and school on rewired rings, and each
// day what the ill give off taken from the hazard of whom they meet
// (transmission.ent): at home through the household, up a tree and back
// down; at work along the ties that are met that day, each tie one edge
// met from either end; and by chance, along the edges of a relation
// that is emptied and filled anew every day, from stubs laid out by a
// proc and paired in an order the day says. Every draw is worked out
// from the seed and what it is for, so one core and all of them give
// the same run to the byte.
// (examples/epidemic/check/city.py holds a city of 100,000 against the
// reference's targets.)
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/epidemic %S/Inputs/epidemic_city.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/epidemic %S/Inputs/epidemic_city.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// The people by the network of their age come to 5,000; a tie for every
// member and every place within reach on its ring.
// CHECK:      panel 80 households 2149 ties 36099
// CHECK-NEXT: networks 607 565 3169 412 247
// CHECK-NEXT: met by chance 17455.0 a day
// Five are infected at the start, and it spreads.
// CHECK-NEXT: day 0: new 5 well 4995 ill 5 recovered 0 dead 0
// CHECK-NEXT: day 10: new 9 well 4965 ill 34 recovered 1 dead 0
// CHECK:      day 40: new 106 well 1365 ill 2779 recovered 849 dead 7
// It ends with nobody ill: who was never infected, recovered or dead.
// CHECK:      day 102: new 0 well 740 ill 0 recovered 4230 dead 30
// CHECK-NOT:  day
